# Local Terraform working state - never commit real state or plan output,
# both can contain resource attribute values (some sensitive) in plaintext.
# Use a remote backend (S3/GCS/Azure Blob + state locking) for anything
# beyond a single operator's laptop - see each cloud subdirectory's
# README.md for the exact backend config block to add.
**/.terraform/
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
*.tfplan
crash.log
crash.*.log
override.tf
override.tf.json
*_override.tf
*_override.tf.json

# .terraform.lock.hcl SHOULD be committed (pins exact provider versions) -
# deliberately not listed here.

# Real tfvars almost always carry account-specific (sometimes sensitive)
# values - commit only *.tfvars.example files.
*.tfvars
!*.tfvars.example
